            "target_entity_type": "ClimateZone",
            "paragraph": "Semi-arid mountain areas are so sensitive to climate change that a small change in temperature and precipitation can quickly result in a large change in water availability due to a rise in evaporative demand and a strong topographic control on hydroclimate [1]. In Morocco, observational data shows a continuous trend of warming since the second half of the 20th century, with a reported increase of around 0.33 \u00b0C/decade (1.1 \u00b0C for 1984-2016) and tendency of decreased precipitation after taking into account the evaporative demand [2].",
